\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One spin value moved across a periodic rectangle}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Choose two directions on a complex spin plane. The first
exchanges two orthonormal basis vectors, and the second fixes
the first vector and negates the second. With the trivial
scalar fiber the grading #{C=\ui\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2}
has square one and anticommutes with both directions.
On a rectangle of periods #{3} and #{5} a field supported
at #{(1,2)} with value #{v} is carried to a field supported
at #{(2,3)} with value #{Cv} by
[graded total inversion](fdip-019C). Each reflected coordinate
is read in its own period. Applying the same inversion again
returns the initial field.}
